---
import {
  BACKLOG_ROWS,
  BACKLOG_TOTAL,
  INITIAL_STATE,
  PLANNED_SPRINT_ROWS,
  plural,
  SPRINT,
  tallyBoard,
  TOTAL_POINTS,
  type BacklogRow,
} from '@lib/features/sprints-kanban-boards';

const resolved = tallyBoard(INITIAL_STATE).resolvedPoints;
const plannedPoints = PLANNED_SPRINT_ROWS.reduce((sum, row) => sum + (row.points ?? 0), 0);
const hiddenBacklog = BACKLOG_TOTAL.issues - BACKLOG_ROWS.length;
const typeClass = (row: BacklogRow) => ({ Bug: 'l-bug', Feature: 'l-feature', Task: 'l-task' })[row.type];
---

<section class="border-t border-line bg-app" aria-labelledby="plan-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <h2 id="plan-title" class="h2">
        From an ordered backlog to a running sprint.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5 max-w-[46ch]">
        The backlog is every issue in no sprint. You decide what moves into the next one; nothing is planned for you.
      </p>
      <ol class="steps-list mt-8 prose text-base">
        <li>
          <strong>Order the backlog.</strong> Drag a row by its grip, or focus the grip and use <kbd>Space</kbd>, the
          arrow keys and <kbd>Space</kbd> again. The board shows cards in the same order.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Move work into a planned sprint.</strong> Drop rows into it, or bring over every unresolved issue of
          the running sprint when you create the next one.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Set a goal and points.</strong> The goal is Markdown. Story points are whole numbers from 0 to 999; an
          issue without them reads <em>Not estimated</em>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Start it.</strong> It starts on the day you start it and keeps its planned end date, which drives the
          days-left countdown. One sprint runs at a time in each project.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <figure class="lg:col-span-7">
      <div class="panel overflow-hidden">
        <div class="pane-bar">
          <span class="mono text-xs">ACME</span>
          <span class="sep">/</span>
          <span class="text-fg">Backlog</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bl-section">
          <p class="bl-head">
            <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">
              ›
            </span>
            <span class="text-fg font-medium">{SPRINT.name}</span>
            <span class="pill">Active</span>
            <span class="bl-meta">
              {`${SPRINT.dates} · ${SPRINT.daysLeft} days left · ${resolved} of ${TOTAL_POINTS} points resolved`}
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bl-section">
          <p class="bl-head">
            <span class="chev open" aria-hidden="true">
              ›
            </span>
            <span class="text-fg font-medium">Sprint 09</span>
            <span class="pill">Planned</span>
            <span class="bl-meta">
              {`19 Oct – 30 Oct 2026 · ${plural(PLANNED_SPRINT_ROWS.length, 'issue')} · ${plannedPoints} points`}
            </span>
          </p>
          <p class="bl-goal">Goal: members can manage invitations without asking an admin.</p>
          <ul>
            {PLANNED_SPRINT_ROWS.map(row => (
              <li class="bl-row">
                <span class="grip" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span class="key">{row.key}</span>
                <span class="title">{row.title}</span>
                <span class:list={['badge', typeClass(row)]} title={row.type}>
                  <span aria-hidden="true">{row.type.charAt(0)}</span>
                  <span class="sr-only">{row.type}</span>
                </span>
                <span class="pts">{row.points === null ? 'Not estimated' : plural(row.points, 'point')}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bl-section">
          <p class="bl-head">
            <span class="chev open" aria-hidden="true">
              ›
            </span>
            <span class="text-fg font-medium">Backlog</span>
            <span class="bl-meta">{`${plural(BACKLOG_TOTAL.issues, 'issue')} · ${BACKLOG_TOTAL.points} points`}</span>
          </p>
          <p class="querybar bl-query">
            <span class="q">#Unresolved</span>
            <span class="count">{plural(BACKLOG_TOTAL.issues, 'issue')}</span>
          </p>
          <ul>
            {BACKLOG_ROWS.map(row => (
              <li class="bl-row">
                <span class="grip" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span class="key">{row.key}</span>
                <span class="title">{row.title}</span>
                <span class:list={['badge', typeClass(row)]} title={row.type}>
                  <span aria-hidden="true">{row.type.charAt(0)}</span>
                  <span class="sr-only">{row.type}</span>
                </span>
                <span class:list={['pts', { none: row.points === null }]}>
                  {row.points === null ? 'Not estimated' : plural(row.points, 'point')}
                </span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <p class="bl-more">{plural(hiddenBacklog, 'more issue')}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mt-4 text-xs text-fg-3">
        The running sprint comes first, then each planned sprint, then the backlog. The query above the backlog narrows
        only the backlog. Hand-drawn product view with fictional data.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  kbd {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    padding: 0 5px;
  }
  .bl-section + .bl-section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .bl-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px 8px;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 20px;
  }
  .chev {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 10px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .chev.open {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }
  .pill {
    font-size: 11.5px;
    line-height: 18px;
    padding: 0 6px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    background: var(--bg-inset);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .bl-meta {
    flex-basis: 100%;
    padding-left: 18px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .bl-meta {
      flex-basis: auto;
      margin-left: auto;
      padding-left: 0;
    }
  }
  .bl-goal {
    padding: 0 16px 10px 34px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 18px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .bl-query {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    height: 36px;
  }
  .bl-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 10px 60px minmax(0, 1fr) 18px auto;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 36px;
    padding: 7px 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 18px;
  }
  .grip {
    width: 6px;
    height: 12px;
    background-image: radial-gradient(var(--border-strong) 1px, transparent 1.2px);
    background-size: 3px 4px;
  }
  .pts {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-align: right;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .pts.none {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .bl-row {
      grid-template-columns: 10px 56px minmax(0, 1fr) 18px;
      row-gap: 2px;
    }
    .bl-row .pts {
      grid-column: 3 / 5;
      grid-row: 2;
      text-align: left;
    }
  }
  .bl-more {
    padding: 9px 16px 12px 36px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .l-feature {
    --c-bg: var(--palette-blue-bg);
    --c-fg: var(--palette-blue-fg);
  }
  .l-task {
    --c-bg: var(--palette-gray-bg);
    --c-fg: var(--palette-gray-fg);
  }
</style>
